133	// fixed discount), and can be sent; a change to a sent invoice with no payments puts it back to
134	// draft, and once paid anything the server refuses further changes. A sent invoice takes payments
135	// until nothing is due, less than $1.00 left being written off; the panel lists them with what has
136	// been paid, what is still due and what was written off. The
137	// server refuses a payment on a draft, or dated after today or before the issue date; what a payment
138	// pays beyond what is due is held on the client's account as credit.
139	// The panel shows the invoice's RF payment reference; a payment may quote one, which must pass the
140	// ISO 11649 check and be this invoice's. When parts of a payment are filled in on the list, the
141	// payment is spread over those invoices instead; each payment shows how much of it went here.
142	// A sent invoice with no payments can be voided; the server refuses to void a draft or one with
143	// payments, and refuses any payment or change to a void invoice. A payment can be reversed (a bounced
144	// cheque): it is undone on every invoice it was applied to and never counts again. Any invoice can
145	// be duplicated into a new draft for the same client, which then opens. A draft's due date can be set
146	// by hand, from its issue date to 120 days after it; it is kept when the invoice is sent, and the
147	// server refuses to send it once that date is past. A draft can hold back retention, a percentage of
148	// the grand total (0 to 20); while held it is not part of the amount due, and once nothing else is due
